A '''gang''' of three [[Trandoshan]] [[bounty hunter]]s in matching uniforms were in operation shortly after the fall of the [[Galactic Empire]]. The gang ambushed the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] on the [[planet]] [[Arvala-7]] in an attempt to kill [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] which the Mandalorian was carrying with him. However, the three Trandoshans were quickly defeated by their opponent who escaped with Grogu.

==History==
[[File:Djarin-Trandoshan-TMS1C2.png|thumb|left|250px|The Trandoshans fight the bounty hunter Din Djarin]]
In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate|S1}}</ref> the [[Trandoshan]]s traveled to [[Arvala-7]] to attempt to capture "[[Din Grogu|Grogu]],"<ref name="Chapter 2" /> upon which "[[The Client]]" had placed a [[bounty]].<ref name="Chapter 1: The Mandalorian">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref> The Trandoshans used a [[tracking fob]] to track the child and discovered it in the possession the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]]. The gang attempted to ambush the Mandalorian with slaver blades, but he defeated them after a brief skirmish. One of the Trandoshans charged toward Grogu and tried to kill it, but The Mandalorian shot and disintegrated him, after which he discovered the dead bounty hunter's tracking fob.<ref name="Chapter 2" />

{{Stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Trandoshan bounty hunter gang were first teased in the second official trailer for the [[Jon Favreau]]'s television show ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''.<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|XmI7WKrAtqs|The Mandalorian &ndash; Official Trailer 2 &#124; Disney+ &#124; Streaming Nov. 12|sw_url=video/trailer-2-the-mandalorian}}</ref> The gang first appeared in "[[Chapter 2: The Child]]," the second episode of the show, which was directed by [[Rick Famuyiwa]]<ref name="Chapter 2" /> and aired on [[November 15]] [[2019]].<ref name="Episode Amount">{{WebCite|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/star-wars-new-mandalorian-details-footage-unveiled-1201931|text='The Mandalorian': Jon Favreau Teases Disney+ Series at Star Wars Celebration|author=Aaron Couch & Graeme McMillan|date=2018-12-10|archivedate=20191109001233}}</ref>

